# Flume / lab dump post-process

## Folders

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `OSU_SSI_BRIDGE_DATA/` | Junction → Shared Drive `…/2026-08-21-OSU-SSI-Bridge/opensees_data` — **read-only** dumps |
| Shared Drive archive | `G:\Shared drives\Simpson team\Test Data\2026-08-21-OSU-SSI-Bridge\` (`opensees_data/` + `README.txt`) |
| `OSU_SSI_BRIDGE_DATA_LOCAL/` | Local working mirror (gitignored). Under `opensees_data/`: run dumps, `Simulink/`, `mat_extract/`, manifest. Plots under `plots/`. |
| `OSU_SSI_BRIDGE_DATA_LOCAL/plots/` | All post-process PNGs (`<run>/`, `compare/<group>/`) |
| `plot/opensees_data/TestMatrix_lab_runs.csv` | Curated as-run matrix (git-tracked). Edit by hand; not regenerated. Working copy may also sit at `LOCAL/TestMatrix_lab_runs.csv`. |
| `plot/opensees_data/mat_run_map.json` | Simulink `.mat` ↔ OpenSees run folder dictionary (git-tracked; copied into local tree on sync) |

List runs from the junction / Shared Drive `opensees_data` folder (31 run dirs + `Simulink/`).

**Read-only rule:** never leave `plots/` (or other outputs) inside a Drive dump folder. `PlotEQParallel.py` auto-routes lab dumps to `OSU_SSI_BRIDGE_DATA_LOCAL/plots/<run>/`. If a Drive-side `plots/` appears, delete it after copying. Do not write recorder dumps into `LOCAL/plots/`.

**Local backup:** before/while post-processing, run `python plot/SyncLabBackup.py`. It copies new/changed Drive files into `OSU_SSI_BRIDGE_DATA_LOCAL/opensees_data/` (skips `plots/`) and extracts `data` + `*OS` from new Simulink mats to `…/opensees_data/mat_extract/*.npz`. Re-run whenever Drive has more data.

## Infer from the dump — not from the CSV

Lab runs may ignore `TestMatrix.csv` / `Overrides.tcl` / folder-name hints (`r+01`, `np8`, …). **Never** take `Number of Procs`, soil profile, boundary, element type, integrator, or duration from the matrix as ground truth for post-process.

Read what the files say:

1. **Parallel vs serial** — `window_meta.txt.0` (and `*.out.$pid`) → `PlotEQParallel.py`; plain `window_nodes.txt` / `window_meta.txt` → `PlotEQ.py`.
2. **`np`** — `np` in `window_meta.txt.0`; confirm ranks `0 .. np-1` exist for meta (PlotEQParallel already does this). Sparse recorder shards on some ranks are normal (lean dump).
3. **Model knobs** — same meta: `soilProfile`, `soilBoundary`, `soilEleType`, `pierHinge`, `pileEleType`, `recordersON`, `Trec`, `freeVibT`, `dtAnalysis`, `gmVelFile`, …
4. **What was recorded** — glob the folder (`pier_node_*.out.*`, `Elmt*_ctrlDsp.out`, springs, quads). Plot only what is present; do not assume every TestMatrix instrument is there.
5. **Incomplete uploads** — if meta/disp/hinge files are missing, skip and report; recheck later (Drive sync). Incomplete *analyses* (t_last ≪ Trec) are still plotted.

Folder names may include `Storm_Wave` / `Big_Tsunami` (wave-catalog label from the
matrix). That is the wave type in the campaign, not “wave-only”: the OpenSees
record is earthquake motion (then free vib / continued time), with the flume wave
timed relative to the EQ per the lab. Infer loading from the dump and lab notes,
not from the folder nickname alone.

## Scripts

Always use the plotters in `plot/`:

- OpenSeesMP: `python plot/PlotEQParallel.py <eqOutDir>`  
  Lab dumps → `OSU_SSI_BRIDGE_DATA_LOCAL/plots/<run>/` automatically (or `--plots-out DIR`).
- Serial: `python plot/PlotEQ.py <eqOutDir>` (prefer copying PNGs out of Drive if that path is a lab dump).
- Pier-top ux overlays: `python plot/PlotEQCompareRuns.py`  
  → `OSU_SSI_BRIDGE_DATA_LOCAL/plots/compare/<group>/hist_ux_*.png`  
  Groups from `TestMatrix_lab_runs.csv` model knobs (mesh, soil, element, constitutive,
  hybrid/hold, non-default Rayleigh ξ) — not solver/`np`. Same physical model stays
  in one folder so overlays are fair.  
  → `hist_ux_*_realtime.png`: Simulink **meaSigOS** (no OpenSees interp); primary =
  prototype, secondary = model (λ = 2.4).  
  Mat ↔ run map: `plot/opensees_data/mat_run_map.json`
- Backup + mat extract: `python plot/SyncLabBackup.py`
- Simulink *OS: `python plot/PlotMatOS.py`  
  → per run: `hist_os_com.png`, `hist_os_state.png`, `hist_os_tar_com_mea.png`  
  → compare: `OSU_SSI_BRIDGE_DATA_LOCAL/plots/compare/<group>/hist_os_com.png`, `hist_os_state.png`

On this machine prefer Anaconda `python.exe` if `python` is the Windows Store stub.

## When the user asks to post-process

1. List run folders under `OSU_SSI_BRIDGE_DATA/` (junction → Shared Drive archive).
2. Run `SyncLabBackup.py` if Drive has new/changed files (or always — it skips unchanged).
3. Skip runs that already have PNGs under `OSU_SSI_BRIDGE_DATA_LOCAL/plots/<run>/` unless re-plotting.
4. Inspect meta + file list; choose PlotEQ vs PlotEQParallel from the dump.
5. Run the plotter on that dump folder (lab path → plots land in `LOCAL/plots`).
6. Remove any accidental Drive-side `<run>/plots/` after a successful copy.
7. Refresh compare overlays (`PlotEQCompareRuns.py`) when several runs exist.
8. Sanity-check from the data: last sample vs meta `Trec`, no NaN/Inf, pier top ux, hinge, OpenFresco channels if present. Report oddities.

Do not commit dump files, `OSU_SSI_BRIDGE_DATA/`, `OSU_SSI_BRIDGE_DATA_LOCAL/`, or bulky plot PNGs.
